{
  "id": "u08-l01",
  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "I do / you do",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bengali verbs change their ending for the person, and the endings are very regular. Here is **করা** (*kora*, 'to do'):\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| আমি / আমরা | **করি** (*kori*) |\n| তুই | **করিস** (*korish*) |\n| তুমি / তোমরা | **করো** (*koro*) |\n| আপনি / তিনি | **করেন** (*koren*) |\n| সে / তারা | **করে** (*kore*) |\n\nThere's no difference between singular and plural in the verb: আমি করি, আমরা করি. And polite 'you' and polite 'he/she' share **-েন**.\n\nMany everyday actions are **noun + করা**: **কাজ করা** 'to work' (lit. 'do work'). **আপনি কী করেন?** 'What do you do?' is how people ask about your job.\n\nUseful reactions: **সত্যি?** \"Really?\" and **আসলে…** \"Actually…\".",
  "vocab": [
